# =========================

# Curie - Git Ignore

# =========================

# ---------- Python ----------

**pycache**/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# Virtual environments

.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# Python tooling

.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ---------- Secrets / Configuration ----------

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local configuration files

config.local.*
secrets.*
credentials.*
*_secret.*
*_credentials.*

# ---------- Curie Runtime Data ----------

# Local SQLite database containing Curie's memory, chat history,

# user facts, habits, and brain-dump data.

memory.db
memory.db-*
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Logs

*.log
logs/

# ---------- Temporary / Generated Files ----------

tmp/
temp/
*.tmp
*.temp

# Audio generated during runtime

*.wav
*.mp3
*.ogg

# ---------- Arduino ----------

# Arduino IDE build output

build/
*.elf
*.hex
*.bin
*.eep
*.map

# Arduino temporary files

arduino_build_*/
arduino_cache_*/

# ---------- VS Code ----------

.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json

# ---------- Platform / OS ----------

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Windows thumbnails

ehthumbs.db

# ---------- Archives ----------

# Ignore exported archives unless deliberately placed

# in the releases directory.

*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz

!releases/*.zip

# ---------- CAD ----------

# Temporary CAD files

*.bak
*.tmp
*.lock
*.lck

# CAD autosave / recovery

~$*
*.autosave

# ---------- Personal / Local Files ----------

notes_private/
private/
local/

````

**One important thing:** don't put `memory.db` on GitHub. Your code explicitly stores chat history and user facts in that SQLite database, so it could contain personal information.

And definitely don't commit API keys. Your current `main.py` has configuration fields for the Groq and Cartesia credentials, so I'd make sure the actual keys are blank before uploading the code.

For the repo, I'd also add a tiny **`.env.example`** showing what someone needs to configure without containing your actual keys:

```text
GROQ_API_KEY=
CARTESIA_API_KEY=
CARTESIA_VOICE_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN=
````

That way someone cloning Curie immediately knows what credentials they need, without you accidentally publishing yours.
